    {
      "id": "tiktok-7710274027033660694",
      "number": 7,
      "title": "You don't need help. You need company. Same 10 tasks. Alone, you pick up your phone after the first one. Then someone sits down next to you, doesn't say a word, doesn't touch your work, and suddenly you can't stop. That's called body doubling. An ADHD brain often struggles to start on its own, and another person in the room quietly gives it the push it's missing. It's why you clean faster when a friend is over and work better in a café. Try it today: ask someone to sit with you for 25 minutes, in person or on a video call. They do their thing, you do yours. Same tasks. Not alone.",
      "caption": "You don't need help. You need company. Same 10 tasks. Alone, you pick up your phone after the first one. Then someone sits down next to you, doesn't say a word, doesn't touch your work, and suddenly you can't stop. That's called body doubling. An ADHD brain often struggles to start on its own, and another person in the room quietly gives it the push it's missing. It's why you clean faster when a friend is over and work better in a café. Try it today: ask someone to sit with you for 25 minutes, in person or on a video call. They do their thing, you do yours. Same tasks. Not alone.",
